  "meta": {
    "name": "WFC Circuits",
    "createdAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z",
    "modifiedAt": "2026-10-09T00:00:00.000Z"
  },
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "wf_c",
      "defType": "meta/comment",
      "position": {
        "x": 0,
        "y": -264
      },
      "params": {
        "text": "Wave function collapse\n\nThe Tiles node in `wfc` mode fills the grid with tiles whose edges must match: `sockets` lists each tile as four characters for its north, east, south and west edges (`0` = nothing, `1` = a pipe), and `*3` makes one three times as likely. Every tile is tried in its four turns. Cell by cell, the most constrained one is settled and its neighbours narrowed down — and with `closed` on, no pipe runs off the grid (`1000`, a dead end, is the only way to stop short).\n\nEach kind of tile takes its own colour. Change `seed`, or edit the sockets (try removing the tees `1110`).",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 200
      },
      "portValues": {
        "text": "Wave function collapse\n\nThe Tiles node in `wfc` mode fills the grid with tiles whose edges must match: `sockets` lists each tile as four characters for its north, east, south and west edges (`0` = nothing, `1` = a pipe), and `*3` makes one three times as likely. Every tile is tried in its four turns. Cell by cell, the most constrained one is settled and its neighbours narrowed down — and with `closed` on, no pipe runs off the grid (`1000`, a dead end, is the only way to stop short).\n\nEach kind of tile takes its own colour. Change `seed`, or edit the sockets (try removing the tees `1110`).",
        "width": 520,
        "height": 200
      }
    },
